    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:reflecting_telescope",
      "title": "Reflecting Telescope",
      "text": "A mirror under a dome, its slit open to the night. The bigger the mirror and the longer the exposure, the fainter the stars it records - on a clear, dark night, under open sky.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Works only at night, with open sky above the slit and no rain. Set the aperture and the exposure: the limiting magnitude rises with both, falls under a bright Moon, and suffers from the seeing - better the higher the telescope stands. Very short exposures freeze the seeing for sharp planetary plates. Every plate gives Insight."
    },
